{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Mordecai wrote.</b> Alone, to establish it in the following year, and likewise every year, the rejoicing of the days of Purim. The meaning of \"on the days on which the Jews rested\" is that the reckoning of our years is calculated at the end of the cycle in a solar year, but our months follow the moon. So the meaning of \"on the days\" is that the days will be close in proportion to the first days on which the Purim fell, and this is possible for us through the addition of a second Adar; therefore Scripture needed to say \"and the month which was turned.\" And it shall always be in the month adjacent to Nisan, whether in a simple or intercalated year. The commentators said that the meaning of \"and the month\" concerns second Adar, and others said that \"as the days\" means the fourteenth and the fifteenth, and if so it should have said \"and in the month,\" not \"and the month.\""], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:23.343690587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}